    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The prime factorization of $24$ is $2^3 \\cdot 3^1$. We can write $24$ as a product of two factors $a$ and $b$ in the following way:\n\n\\[ (a \\cdot b) = a \\cdot b \\cdot 1 \\cdot 1 = a \\cdot b \\cdot 2^{1} \\cdot 3^{1} \\]\n\nTo count the total number of factors of $24$, we can consider the sum of $a$ and $b$ as follows:\n\n\\[ a = 2^{k} \\cdot 3^{m} \\]\n\\[ b = 2^{n} \\cdot 3^{p} \\]\n\nwhere $1 \\leq a$ and $1 \\leq b$, and we have $n + m = 3$ and $k + p = 1.$\n\nSince there are $1! = 1$ options for the prime factors of $24$ (since $1 \\cdot 2, 2 \\cdot 1, 2, 1, 1, 2, 1, 2$ are the same), the total number of factors of $24$ is $\\boxed{6}$.",
